  "summary": "A Flock Safety ALPR camera in Granite Falls, Washington was destroyed on Tuesday evening, and the Granite Falls Police Department is investigating with no suspects in custody. The article notes Granite Falls operates seven Flock cameras and contextualizes the vandalism amid growing pushback, citing recent contract cancellations by Lynnwood, Mountlake Terrace, and Edmonds after reports of federal immigration access.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "A Flock Safety camera was destroyed in Granite Falls on Tuesday evening, the Snohomish County Sheriff's Office confirmed in an email to The Daily Herald on Wednesday.",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "Agencies across the country have seen their cameras vandalized in recent months as concern over the technology grows.",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    },
    {
      "quote": "Since December 2025, Lynnwood, Mountlake Terrace and Edmonds have canceled their contracts with Flock Safety following reports of federal immigration enforcement accessing local networks.",
      "paragraph_idx": 10
    }
  ],
